  "facts": [
    "The Queensboro Bridge, opened March 30, 1909, was the longest cantilever span in North America until 1917, stretching 3,725 feet across the East River and towering up to 140 feet above high water.",
    "Renamed in 2011 after former mayor Ed Koch, the bridge still retains its original nickname, the 59th Street Bridge, a title that sparked controversy among Queens residents who felt it overlooked their borough.",
    "With two levels, the lower deck once carried trolley tracks and now supports four vehicular lanes, a bike lane, and a pedestrian walkway, while the upper deck hosts two lanes of traffic and a high‑occupancy vehicle lane during rush hour."
  ],
